1
00:00:01,650 --> 00:00:05,711
过去，人类最大的梦想，是改变世界。
In the past, humanity's greatest dream was to change the world.

2
00:00:05,811 --> 00:00:08,811
未来，人类可能开始改变自己。
In the future, humanity may begin to change itself.

3
00:00:13,711 --> 00:00:20,493
几千年来，饥荒、瘟疫和战争，一直是人类最大的三个敌人。
For thousands of years, famine, plague and war were humanity's three greatest enemies.

4
00:00:20,693 --> 00:00:26,052
而今天，死于吃得太多的人，比死于吃得太少的人还多；
Today, more people die from eating too much than from eating too little;

5
00:00:26,152 --> 00:00:29,753
死于衰老的人，比死于传染病的人还多；
more die of old age than of infectious disease;

6
00:00:29,853 --> 00:00:35,836
自杀的人，比死于士兵、恐怖分子和罪犯之手的人加起来还多。
and more people take their own lives than are killed by soldiers, terrorists and criminals combined.

7
00:00:35,876 --> 00:00:39,430
如今，糖比火药更危险。
Sugar is now more dangerous than gunpowder.

8
00:00:39,470 --> 00:00:44,195
当旧的威胁退去，人类开始为自己设定新的目标：
As the old threats recede, humanity is setting itself new goals:

9
00:00:44,295 --> 00:00:48,686
长生不死、幸福快乐、化身为神。
immortality, bliss and divinity.

10
00:00:51,186 --> 00:00:54,228
过去，人类接受自然赋予的生命。
In the past, humans accepted the life that nature gave them.

11
00:00:54,328 --> 00:00:57,136
未来，人类可能开始设计生命。
In the future, humans may begin to design life.

12
00:00:57,236 --> 00:00:59,929
赫拉利设想了三条“升级”之路：
Harari sees three paths to "upgrading" ourselves:

13
00:01:00,029 --> 00:01:04,416
改写基因，与机器融合，创造非有机的生命。
rewriting our genes, merging with machines, creating non-organic life.

14
00:01:04,516 --> 00:01:10,386
疾病、衰老，甚至身体本身，都可能成为可以修改的对象。
Disease, ageing, even the body itself, may all become things we can edit.

15
00:01:10,686 --> 00:01:12,713
如果意识可以被复制，
If consciousness could be copied,

16
00:01:12,813 --> 00:01:14,957
如果记忆可以被保存，
if memories could be preserved,

17
00:01:15,057 --> 00:01:17,548
如果生命可以无限延续，
if life could go on forever,

18
00:01:17,648 --> 00:01:19,942
我们还是原来的自己吗？
would we still be who we were?

19
00:01:22,442 --> 00:01:25,374
人类第一次创造了一种新的智能。
For the first time, humans have created a new kind of intelligence.

20
00:01:25,474 --> 00:01:28,199
它不需要生命，却能够学习。
It needs no life, yet it can learn.

21
00:01:28,299 --> 00:01:31,643
智能，正在与意识分道扬镳。
Intelligence is decoupling from consciousness.

22
00:01:31,743 --> 00:01:33,351
而生命科学告诉我们：
And the life sciences tell us:

23
00:01:33,651 --> 00:01:37,652
生物本身就是算法，生命就是数据处理。
organisms are algorithms, and life is data processing.

24
00:01:37,752 --> 00:01:41,659
几百年来，人文主义告诉我们：倾听你自己。
For centuries, humanism has told us: listen to yourself.

25
00:01:41,759 --> 00:01:44,157
可当算法比你自己更了解你，
But when algorithms know you better than you know yourself,

26
00:01:44,257 --> 00:01:48,707
从走哪条路、读哪本书，到和谁共度一生，
from the road you take and the books you read to the person you marry,

27
00:01:48,807 --> 00:01:52,628
权威，就会从人类转移到算法手中。
authority will shift from humans to algorithms.

28
00:01:52,728 --> 00:01:57,976
当机器开始理解世界，人类的位置将发生什么变化？
When machines begin to understand the world, what becomes of humanity's place?

29
00:01:58,376 --> 00:02:02,741
但还有一个问题：这样的未来，会属于每个人吗？
But one question remains: will such a future belong to everyone?

30
00:02:02,841 --> 00:02:04,760
当算法承担越来越多工作，
As algorithms take on more and more work,

31
00:02:05,060 --> 00:02:09,164
一些人可能难以在经济体系中重新找到位置。
some people may struggle to find a place in the economy.

32
00:02:09,264 --> 00:02:12,381
赫拉利将这种风险称为“无用阶级”。
Harari calls this risk "the useless class".

33
00:02:12,481 --> 00:02:15,244
这里的“无用”，指劳动可能不再被需要，
"Useless" here means their labour may no longer be needed,

34
00:02:15,544 --> 00:02:18,484
绝不意味着人失去了价值。
never that people have lost their worth.

35
00:02:18,584 --> 00:02:23,755
如果少数人获得升级生命的能力，更多人却被留在身后，
If a few gain the power to upgrade life while many are left behind,

36
00:02:23,855 --> 00:02:28,291
人类可能第一次在生物学意义上，分裂成不同的阶层。
humankind may, for the first time, split into biological castes.

37
00:02:28,391 --> 00:02:30,640
当我们追问人类能成为什么，
As we ask what humans can become,

38
00:02:30,940 --> 00:02:34,358
也必须追问：谁能共享这个未来？
we must also ask: who will share this future?

39
00:02:36,758 --> 00:02:41,532
与此同时，一种新的信仰正在兴起：数据主义。
Meanwhile, a new creed is rising: Dataism.

40
00:02:41,632 --> 00:02:44,232
它相信，宇宙由数据流构成；
It holds that the universe consists of data flows,

41
00:02:44,532 --> 00:02:48,676
万物的价值，取决于它对数据处理的贡献。
and the value of anything lies in its contribution to data processing.

42
00:02:48,776 --> 00:02:53,649
在这张巨网里，智人也许只是一个正在过时的算法。
In this vast web, Homo sapiens may be just an obsolete algorithm.

43
00:02:53,849 --> 00:02:58,033
未来最大的挑战，不是机器是否会超越人类，
The greatest challenge ahead is not whether machines will surpass us,

44
00:02:58,133 --> 00:03:01,076
而是当我们拥有创造神的能力，
but whether, once we can create gods,

45
00:03:01,126 --> 00:03:05,273
是否仍然知道如何成为人？
will we still know how to be human?

46
00:03:05,313 --> 00:03:08,399
智人，也许正在走向“神人”。
Homo sapiens may be on its way to becoming Homo Deus.

47
00:03:08,899 --> 00:03:11,460
这不是预言，而是可能。
These are not prophecies, but possibilities.

48
00:03:11,560 --> 00:03:14,835
赫拉利在书的最后，留下了三个问题：
At the end of the book, Harari leaves us three questions:

49
00:03:14,875 --> 00:03:17,703
生物真的只是算法吗？
Are organisms really just algorithms?

50
00:03:17,803 --> 00:03:21,869
智能与意识，哪一个更有价值？
Which is more valuable: intelligence or consciousness?

51
00:03:21,969 --> 00:03:27,003
当算法比我们更了解自己，生活会变成什么样？
What happens when algorithms know us better than we know ourselves?

52
00:03:27,103 --> 00:03:29,468
下一章人类历史，
The next chapter of human history

53
00:03:29,568 --> 00:03:32,742
正在等待我们书写。
is waiting for us to write.

